@api = http://localhost:8501/api

### ---------- Menu ----------

### List active menu items (200)
GET {{api}}/coffees


### ---------- Menu images (R2) ----------

### Upload latte.jpg as the photo for item 1 (201, returns the new imageKey)
### "< ./latte.jpg" sends the file's bytes as the body (path is relative to this file).
POST {{api}}/coffees/1/image
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./latte.jpg

### Wrong file type (400)
POST {{api}}/coffees/1/image
Content-Type: text/plain

this is not an image

### Menu item does not exist (404)
POST {{api}}/coffees/999/image
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./latte.jpg


### ---------- Place an order ----------

### Place an order for item 1 (201, returns the saved order)
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "itemId": 1 }

### itemId is not an integer (400)
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "itemId": "1" }

### Missing body / invalid JSON (400)
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

not json

### Item does not exist (404)
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "itemId": 999 }


### ---------- Check an order ----------

### Get order 1 (200)
GET {{api}}/orders/1

### Order does not exist (404)
GET {{api}}/orders/999

### Bad order id (400)
GET {{api}}/orders/abc


### ---------- Move an order along ----------
### Order: received -> preparing -> ready -> collected
### Send these one at a time, top to bottom.

### received -> preparing (200)
PATCH {{api}}/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedStatus": "received" }

### Send "received" again: order already moved on (409)
PATCH {{api}}/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedStatus": "received" }

### preparing -> ready (200)
PATCH {{api}}/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedStatus": "preparing" }

### ready -> collected (200)
PATCH {{api}}/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedStatus": "ready" }

### "collected" is the last step, there is no next status (400)
PATCH {{api}}/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedStatus": "collected" }

### Order does not exist (404)
PATCH {{api}}/orders/999/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expectedStatus": "received" }


### ---------- CORS check ----------

### Preflight like the browser sends before a PATCH from the page (204)
### Look for Access-Control-Allow-Methods (includes PATCH) and
### Access-Control-Allow-Headers (includes Content-Type) in the response headers.
OPTIONS {{api}}/orders/1/status
Origin: http://localhost:8500
Access-Control-Request-Method: PATCH
Access-Control-Request-Headers: Content-Type
